2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Require pr and merge queue on main
 # uuid: 373158c9-19e5-5f28-b348-0b8e6e247a20
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Prediscussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Every change to `main` arrives through a pull request tested against the tip it joins.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The `manuals` repo had no branch protection on `main`. Changes landed by pushing directly or by manually merging pull requests, with no guarantee that a PR's checks ran against the tip it was about to join.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Run `gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/rulesets/<id> --jq '.rules[].type'` to confirm the rule list carries no `merge_queue` entry, and read below for the merge-method argument.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Require pr and merge queue on main
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2021) 'See `DETAILS.md` for the full argument.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2021) 'See `DETAILS.md` for the full argument.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Two PRs can each pass against an older `main` and then conflict or break the Quarto build once both land. How should changes reach `main` so that every merge is reviewable and tested against the tip it will actually join?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Context and problem statement
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The `manuals` repo had no branch protection on `main`. Changes landed by pushing directly or by manually merging pull requests, with no guarantee that a PR's checks ran against the tip it was about to join. Two PRs can each pass against an older `main` and then conflict or break the Quarto build once both land. How should changes reach `main` so that every merge is reviewable and tested against the tip it will actually join?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Decision drivers
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Every change to `main` should arrive through a pull request, not a direct push.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2021) '- A PR should be validated against the latest `main` before it lands.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2021) '- The team is small, so the process should add little ceremony (no mandatory second reviewer, no enqueue step).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2021) '- The setting should be declarative and recorded, not click-ops folklore.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Considered options
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Leave `main` unprotected (status quo).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Branch protection requiring a pull request only.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2021) '- A repository ruleset requiring a pull request plus a merge queue.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2021) '- A repository ruleset requiring a pull request plus strict required status checks.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Decision outcome
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Chosen option: a repository ruleset requiring a pull request plus strict required status checks, because it keeps `main` PR-only and tests each change against the current tip without forcing a second reviewer or an enqueue step.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The ruleset targets the default branch with these rules:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Block branch deletion and non-fast-forward pushes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Require a pull request, with `0` required approvals (review is allowed, not mandated).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Require status check `prek`, with `strict_required_status_checks_policy` set to `true`, so a PR whose branch is behind `main` updates and re-runs its checks before it merges.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Alongside the ruleset, the repository sets `delete_branch_on_merge`, so a merged PR's source branch is removed automatically.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2021) '### The merge method
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2021) '`allow_squash_merge` and `allow_rebase_merge` are both `false`, leaving `allow_merge_commit` as the only way a pull request can land. Auto-merge stays enabled; with the other two off it can only produce a merge commit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2021) 'This is not a preference for more commits. A split costs CI linearly: every commit must pass on its own, so a branch of `n` commits is `n` verifications and not one, paid again on every push while the branch lives. Against that a split buys understandability, review reads one idea at a time, and `git bisect` lands on a change small enough to read rather than on a whole feature.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The trade is real in both directions and it is decided per branch. Most branches are one idea and should be squashed locally before the pull request is final; the doc-gate port in `fabric#52` was collapsed from four commits to one for exactly that reason. A split earns its keep only when the concerns are independent, as in `fabric#54`, where a new gate and a documentation correction had nothing to do with each other and each passed alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2021) 'So the question the setting answers is not how many commits a branch should have. It is who decides, and when:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Squashing at merge time decides for every branch, after review, and collapses the series that was deliberately kept along with the ones that were not. The author already had the cheaper option, `git rebase -i` before marking the PR ready, and it costs the same CI either way, because the squashed branch is verified once as one commit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2021) '- A squash or a rebase also gives the merge a new SHA, so the branch tip is not an ancestor of the default branch afterwards. The documented post-merge check reads exactly that, and reported three complete merges as unmerged in a single day.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The second could be answered by comparing trees instead of commits, and that change is worth making anyway because history already holds squashed merges. It does not answer the first.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2021) '### Why not a merge queue
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The earlier form of this decision required a `merge_queue` rule. The queue serializes entries and builds each against the branch tip, which is worth its cost on a repo with enough concurrent PRs that rebasing by hand becomes the bottleneck. This repo merges documentation changes a few at a time, and the queue charged for capacity it never used:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Every merge needs an explicit enqueue step, and the queue snapshots the PR head at enqueue time, so a late fix races the merge and can be orphaned.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2021) '- `gh pr merge --delete-branch` fails while a queue is enabled ("Cannot use `-d` or `--delete-branch` when merge queue enabled"), so branch cleanup has to move to the repo-level `delete_branch_on_merge` setting.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2021) '- The `merge_queue` rule names no CI job on its own. A ruleset carrying `pull_request` + `merge_queue` and no `required_status_checks` rule merges a PR through the queue even when every check on it failed. This bit two dependent repos (`taskweft/taskweft`, `taskweft/nif`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The strict `required_status_checks` policy keeps the property the queue was there for, a change is tested against the tip it joins, and the enqueue discipline goes away with it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Good: `main` only changes through PRs, and a PR behind the tip updates and re-runs its checks before it lands.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Good: the configuration is captured here and reproducible from the ruleset JSON.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Good: merging is a single `gh pr merge` with no enqueue step and no dequeue-to-fix dance.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Bad: solo edits still need a PR.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Bad: with `0` required approvals, the rule enforces process but not review, so an unreviewed PR can still merge.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2021) '- Bad: strict checks re-run on update, so a burst of concurrent PRs costs one extra CI round per PR that falls behind, with no batching.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Confirmation
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The ruleset is active (id `17352485`). `gh api repos/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/multiplayer-fabric-manuals/rulesets` lists it, a direct push to `main` is rejected, and the rule list carries no `merge_queue` entry:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2021) '```sh
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2021) 'gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/rulesets/<id> --jq '.rules[].type'
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2021) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2021) '`gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/rulesets/<id> --jq '.rules[] | select(.type == "required_status_checks")'` returns the rule with the expected job names and `strict_required_status_checks_policy: true`, and a PR with a failing check cannot merge.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2021) '`gh api repos/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/<repo> --jq .delete_branch_on_merge` returns `true`, and the source branch of a merged PR no longer exists.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2021) 'In the RFD repository, ruleset `23145233` carries `deletion`, `pull_request` and `merge_queue`, and no `required_status_checks` rule (operator, 2026-11-13). As the section on the merge queue says of such a ruleset, the queue merges a pull request whatever `prek` reports. The gate is run on the desk before a pull request is enqueued: both steps of the `prek` job, on the Erlang/OTP and Elixir versions the workflow pins.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The rule was removed while a `prek` job sat queued for 26 minutes with no runner to take it. The command is the one under More information, sent with the rule left out:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2021) '```sh
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2021) 'gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/rulesets/<id> --jq '.rules[].type'
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2021) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2021) 'prints `deletion`, `pull_request` and `merge_queue`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2021) 'More information
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2021) 'The ruleset is edited with `gh api -X PUT repos/<org>/<repo>/rulesets/<id> --input ruleset.json`. The API replaces the whole rule array, so read the current rules first and send back every rule to keep, not only the one being changed:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2021) '```sh
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2021) 'gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/rulesets/<id> --jq '.rules'
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2021) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Job names to require come from a real PR's checks:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2021) '```sh
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2021) 'gh pr checks <PR-number> --repo <org>/<repo>
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2021) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2021) 'and the status-check rule takes the shape:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2021) '```json
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2021) '{
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2021) '  "type": "required_status_checks",
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2021) '  "parameters": {
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2021) '    "strict_required_status_checks_policy": true,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2021) '    "required_status_checks": [{ "context": "<job name from gh pr checks>" }]
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2021) '  }
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2021) '}
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2021) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Change the policy by editing the ruleset rather than protecting the branch through the classic branch-protection API, so the two mechanisms do not overlap.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2021) 'Apply the branch-cleanup setting declaratively:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2021) '```sh
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2021) 'gh api -X PATCH repos/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/<repo> \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2021) '  -F delete_branch_on_merge=true
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2021) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2021  1 LINE
 Text:Written
